.TH TAHTLANG 1 "March 2026" "tahtlang 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tahtlang \- compile TahtLang (.tahta) files to JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tahtlang
.I file.tahta
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tahtlang
compiles
.B .tahta
files into JSON game data for Reigns-style card games.
.PP
TahtLang is a human-readable, line-based DSL designed for
Vim-friendly editing and clean version control diffs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output FILE
Write JSON output to FILE instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-validate
Validate only; print diagnostics and exit without producing output.
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Pretty-print JSON with indentation (default).
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Produce minified JSON without whitespace.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a game file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tahtlang game.tahta --validate
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compile to a JSON file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tahtlang game.tahta -o game.json
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compile to stdout with compact output:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tahtlang game.tahta --compact
.RE
.fi
.SH FILE FORMAT
A
.B .tahta
file consists of entity definitions followed by card definitions.
.SS Entity Definitions
Entities are defined one per line with display name, type prefix, and optional modifiers:
.PP
.nf
.RS
Treasury (counter:treasury, killer)
War Active (flag:war)
Advisor (character:advisor)
.RE
.fi
.SS Type Prefixes
.TP
.B counter:
Numeric value (0\(en100). Add
.B killer
to trigger game over at boundaries.
.TP
.B flag:
Boolean state. Add
.B keep
to persist across reigns.
.TP
.B character:
NPC who delivers cards.
.TP
.B card:
A card definition.
.TP
.B variant:
Character variant (emotion, pose).
.TP
.B settings:
Game settings block.
.SS Card Structure
.PP
.nf
.RS
Tax Proposal (card:tax)
    bearer: character:advisor
    weight: 1.0
    weight: 2.0 when counter:treasury < 30
    require: !flag:war
    lockturn: 10
    > The treasury needs funds.
    * Raise taxes: counter:treasury 20, counter:people -15
    * Cut spending: counter:treasury 10
.RE
.fi
.SS Choice Effects
Counter modification
.RB ( "counter:id N" ),
flag set/clear
.RB ( "+flag:id" ", " "-flag:id" ),
card queuing
.RB ( "card:id" ", " "card:id@N" ),
branching
.RB ( "[card:a, card:b]" ),
and triggers
.RB ( "trigger:type \(dqvalue\(dq" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Parse error, validation error, or file not found.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full syntax reference:
.I docs/spec/syntax.md
in the source repository.
